Firewall penetration testing: steps,methods,and Tools.


Tools :       Nmap
	Telnet/Tracert/Traceroute
	Hping3
	Firewalk network audting tool.



1.Locating The Firewall :-
	Tool:-Hping3
	checkout system Getway or Proxy
	ex. Hping3  -T(for traceroute)  -V  -1(for target) www.example.com



2.Conduction Traceroute
	for linux tool:- traceroute
	ex. traceroute www.example.com
	for windows : tool :tracert
	ex. tracert www.example.com


3.Port Scanning
	tool:Nmap
	nmap  -sS  -p 0-1024(port range) <firewallip>  -T4 
	-sS=SYN flag
	-sV=Service Version
	-T4/T1 =speed for scanning
	both service version and syn flag scan test should be performed by the tester.

4.Banner Grabbing
	tool:- Nmap = nmap  -sV   --script=banner <firewallip>
	           nmap = nmap  -Pn -p 80(give open port number )  -sV --script=banner <firewall ip>
	           curl=curl  -s  -|firewall ip| grep  -e "Server:" or curl   -I <firewall ip:port number>
	          telnet (firewallip)
	          nc  -v (firewall ip)
	          dmitry -b (firewall ip)
5.Firewall Enumration 
	tool=nmap:-nmap -sA (firewall ip)  -T3
		-sA= ACK flag
		-T3= speed for scanning
		port - Open state  - listning mode
		Port - Filter state - blocked by firewall
		Port - Unfillterd state -passing traffic through the port ,but the port is not open 

6.Testing the Firewall Policy
               Test method  - Possible values are 
		Test firewall policy :Source IP/port Destination IP port ,Destination IP /Port and zone that you wish to test 
		Test web policy 
		Include other values also 
		URL 
		Authenticated user 
		Time and Day 

7.Firewalking
	tool:-firewalk
	ex. firewalk  -d543  -i eth0   -n  -pTCP  <system ip > <target ip>
	       firewalk  -S (port range)  -i eth0   -n  -p TCP  <system ip > <target ip>
	-d for destination port
	-i for interface 
	-pTCP for tcp protoall
 	-n for do not resolve ip into host
	
